
@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000

### 1. Welcome endpoint
GET {{baseUrl}}/

### 2. Data model demo
GET {{baseUrl}}/models/demo

### 3. Validate a valid user
POST {{baseUrl}}/models/validate-user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "test_user",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "full_name": "Test User",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 4. Validate a valid blog post
POST {{baseUrl}}/models/validate-post
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My Blog Post",
  "content": "This is a sample blog post with enough content.",
  "author_id": 1,
  "tags": ["test", "demo"]
}

### 5. Get User model JSON schema
GET {{baseUrl}}/models/schema/user

### 6. Get available user roles
GET {{baseUrl}}/models/roles

### 7. Invalid user - password without a digit (Expected: 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/models/validate-user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "test_user",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "passwordonly"
}

### 8. Invalid user - username too short (Expected: 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/models/validate-user
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ab",
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 9. Invalid blog post - invalid tag (Expected: 422)
POST {{baseUrl}}/models/validate-post
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "My Blog Post",
  "content": "This is a sample blog post with enough content.",
  "author_id": 1,
  "tags": ["test", "not valid!"]
}

### 10. Invalid model schema (Expected: 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/models/schema/comment
